  "raw_meta_yaml": "schema_version: 1\n\ncontext:\n  name: ccfits\n  version: \"2.7\"\n  sha256: f63546d2feecbf732cc08aaaa80a2eb5334ada37fb2530181b7363a5dbdeb01a\n\npackage:\n  name: ${{ name|lower }}\n  version: ${{ version }}\n\nsource:\n  url: https://heasarc.gsfc.nasa.gov/FTP/software/fitsio/ccfits/v${{ version }}/CCfits-${{ version }}.tar.gz\n  sha256: ${{ sha256 }}\n  target_directory: CCfits\n  patches:\n    - 0001-Add_missing_m4_macros.patch\n    - 0002-Fix_CXX_LIB_PATH_macro.patch\n    - if: win\n      then: 0003-Pass_no_undefined_libtool.patch\n\nbuild:\n  number: 0\n\nrequirements:\n  build:\n    - ${{ compiler('c') }}\n    - ${{ compiler('cxx') }}\n    - ${{ stdlib('c') }}\n    - make\n    - if: not win\n      then: \n        - automake\n        - autoconf\n        - libtool\n    - if: win\n      then: autotools_clang_conda\n  host:\n    - cfitsio\n  run:\n    - cfitsio\n\ntests:\n  - package_contents:\n      lib:\n        - if: not win\n          then: CCfits\n        - if: win\n          then: \n            - CCfits-*.dll\n            - ccfits.lib\n      include:\n        - CCfits/*\n\nabout:\n  summary: CCfits is an object oriented interface to the cfitsio library. It is designed to make the capabilities of cfitsio available to programmers working in C++. It is written in ANSI C++ and implemented using the C++ Standard Library with namespaces, exception handling, and member template functions.\n  license: CFITSIO\n  license_file: CCfits/License.txt\n  homepage: https://heasarc.gsfc.nasa.gov/fitsio/ccfits/\n  documentation: https://heasarc.gsfc.nasa.gov/fitsio/ccfits/html/index.html\n\nextra:\n  recipe-maintainers:\n    - giacomov\n    - teake\n    - feng1m8\n",
